Aim: Run two threads concurrently.

Algorithm: Start
define two Thread classes
start both
stop.

Program:

class Task extends Thread {
    String msg;
    Task(String m){msg=m;}
    public void run(){
        for(int i=1;i<=3;i++) System.out.println(msg+" "+i);
    }
}
class MultiThreadDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new Task("Thread A").start();
        new Task("Thread B").start();
    }
}

Result: Both threads print their messages three times; order may vary.
